<div class="article about"><section><h1>About Me</h1><div class="prose"><p>I am a software engineer and researcher targeting the <strong>Class of 2027</strong>. My passion lies in dissecting complex systems and rebuilding them with better efficiency and design.</p><p>It began in <strong>2018</strong> with a single line of Python. By <strong>2021</strong>, I was integrating code with hardware, competing in the <em>Beijing Robotics Competition</em> with custom Arduino implementations. This engineering rigor carried into <strong>2023</strong> at the <em>Jinpeng Sci-Tech Forum</em>.</p><p>Recently, I've shifted focus to solving tangible problems. In <strong>2024</strong>, I engineered a Python-based data analysis system to automate business intelligence for <strong>my family's business</strong>. In <strong>2025</strong>, I expanded into mobile development, launching <strong>NightGuard</strong> on the App Store. I also actively engaged with the industry by attending the <em>Vivo Developer Conference</em>, while simultaneously working on experimental Computer Vision research.</p><p>In <strong>2026</strong>, I expanded from building products to building communities. I co-founded <strong>Cobay</strong>, where I organize offline founder meetups and lead development of the website and community product. I also continued exploring the wider builder ecosystem through <em>AWS Summit China</em> and <em>Cafe Cursor Beijing</em>.</p></div></section>
<section><h2>Tech Stack</h2><ul class="stack"><li><strong>Languages:</strong> Swift, Python, Java, Rust, SQL</li><li><strong>Frameworks:</strong> SwiftUI, PyTorch, Astro, Spring Boot</li><li><strong>Tools:</strong> Git, Docker, VS Code, Xcode, Cursor</li></ul></section>
